# Day 29

## Experiment Title

Deploying WordPress and MySQL using Docker Compose


## Objective

To deploy a WordPress application with a MySQL database using Docker Compose.


## Theory

Docker Compose allows multiple related services to be deployed together in a single application environment. WordPress requires a web server and a database service for proper functionality.

Using Docker Compose, both WordPress and MySQL containers can be configured and managed together through a single YAML configuration file. Docker networking enables communication between the application and database containers automatically.


## Requirements

Docker Desktop

Docker Compose

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open Docker Desktop and ensure that Docker services are running properly.

Create a Docker Compose configuration file for WordPress and MySQL services.

Configure database credentials and required ports.

Start the application using Docker Compose.

Verify that both containers are running successfully.

Open the browser and access the WordPress application.


## Output

WordPress and MySQL containers were deployed successfully using Docker Compose.

The application and database containers communicated properly through Docker networking.

The WordPress application was accessible successfully through the browser.


## Result

Successfully deployed and managed a WordPress application with MySQL using Docker Compose.
